owner decision unchanged: gate stays OFF by default; no deploy; R-170 not closed by this batch.

## context: regression found by final review of batch 13
batch 13 (PR #247, merged with owner approval) exempted count-complete lists from the 15-word floor. Side effect: bulleted lists made ONLY of bare success-claim words ("- تم" x3) or abstentions ("- لا أعرف" x3) — previously rejected by the floor alone — became formally acceptable (the ^-anchored whole-text bare-success/abstention checks are defeated by the "- " prefix). This contradicts R-170's explicit purpose. Batch 13b closes the path.

## change (smallest safe; agent_civilization/core/task_fit.py)
new check in assess_prose at the LIST-ITEM level: if EVERY list item (bullet/numbering prefix stripped, trailing punctuation stripped, standard normalization) is a bare success claim or an abstention, the answer is rejected ("a bare success claim, no deliverable" / "abstention, not a completed task"). No word floor re-imposed on correct lists; whole-text checks unchanged; gate default unchanged (off).

